<p>Let’s say I think you stole my wallet. I approach a police officer and tell him my suspicion and describe the evidence that makes me think you have my wallet in your pocket. “Is that his wallet in your pocket?” the cop asks.</p>

<p>“I have no interest in other people’s wallets” would be a rather curious answer.</p>

